# A purge that finished on 10.2.0 leaves L's shard root's marker row initialised,
# with the purged incarnation's generation, and raises no floor (#5697 review, S2).
# The new-build shard root re-seeding the purged tombstone adopts the row: it keeps
# the generation and the initialised flag and skips the first-initialisation fence,
# so L's marker reads initialised with no close above the purged incarnation's
# appends. The #5641 shape, on generations. Moved from the design's
# ReadPositionHonestRoutingAdoptsPredatingMarker.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitRoutingAdoptsPredatingMarker
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: re-creation adopts a marker row that predates the incarnation
PERTURBS: CatchUp

--- FIND
    /\ ~markNew
    /\ LET rc == Max2(rowFloor["s"], Max2(gen["s"], entryRow["s"])) IN
        /\ rc < MaxGen
        /\ rowFloor' = [rowFloor EXCEPT !["s"] = rc]
    /\ mInit' = FALSE
    /\ live' = [live EXCEPT !["s"] = live["s"] /\ caught]
--- REPLACE
    /\ ~markNew
\* MUTATION: the predating marker is adopted: its generation and initialised flag are kept.
    /\ UNCHANGED <<rowFloor, mInit>>
    /\ live' = [live EXCEPT !["s"] = TRUE]
--- END
